{"tool_name":"cabs-flex_2.0","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cabs-flex_2.0","home":"http://biocomp.chem.uw.edu.pl/CABSflex2","summary":"Fast method for predicting protein structure fluctuations that uses a single protein model as the input.","addition_date":"2018-07-02T23:55:36Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:45:39.157751Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cabs-flex_2.0","credit":[{"email":"sekmi@chem.uw.edu.pl","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["Training material"],"url":"http://biocomp.chem.uw.edu.pl/CABSflex2/howto"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein flexibility and motion analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0244"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Protein modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0477"}]}],"name":"CABS-flex 2.0","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"aotamendi.1","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gky356","metadata":{"abstract":"Classical simulations of protein flexibility remain computationally expensive, especially for large proteins. A few years ago, we developed a fast method for predicting protein structure fluctuations that uses a single protein model as the input. The method has been made available as the CABS-flex web server and applied in numerous studies of protein structure-function relationships. Here, we present a major update of the CABS-flex web server to version 2.0. The new features include: extension of the method to significantly larger and multimeric proteins, customizable distance restraints and simulation parameters, contact maps and a new, enhanced web server interface. CABS-flex 2.0 is freely available at http://biocomp.chem.uw.edu.pl/CABSflex2.","authors":[{"name":"Ciemny M.P."},{"name":"Gierut A.M."},{"name":"Kmiecik S."},{"name":"Kolinski A."},{"name":"Kurcinski M."},{"name":"Kuriata A."},{"name":"Oleniecki T."}],"cita